  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the system of equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></math>&nbsp;has infinitely many solutions, then the ordered pair&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>72</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
